{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1566470329,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI2NzI4ODQ4Mw=="},"target":"fbd5c83b7ccfc393569ae22f8208bbab41a605c183e997652c7235e59d6589f3","message":"AFAICS `datalad get` kicks of parallel downloaders by default. On a machine with lots of users that pull lots of files that can quickly grow into a number of connections that trigger firewall rules on the remote end that lead to seemingly broken network connections for any user on such a box.\n\nQ1: git-annex does serial by default and is no problem, we do parallel but go through a control master. Did anyone look into how this would look like from a server perspective? One connection, multiple serverside ssh-processes?\nQ 2: can we centrally reconfigure this behavior to go serial by default, in order to avoid having to instruct each user to use (and obey)  `get -J 1`, if that would be needed? I.o.w. can an admin somehow intervene without having to edit the sources?\n\nSomewhat related to this: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3583","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1566470301,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI1NzYwMDk2MzQ="},"added":["UX"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566478799,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzg5NTA5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3615#issuecomment-523895091"},"message":"Should we add a config variable for that so could be administered if needed?","files":null}]}